/-!
# Weierstrass coordinate change and the henselian cylinder

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé V, Theorem 1.1.1,
Lemmas 1.1.3 and 1.2.3, and proof 2.2.3
(blueprint: lem-per-weierstrass-henselian-cylinder).

We write `s = r - 1` and use the coefficient regrouping `R = D[[T]]`, with
`D = MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ`. The distinguished variable is the outer `PowerSeries.X`.
The ideal `q = (m_D,T)` is written as the inverse image of `m_D` by constant coefficient.
Continuity is for the maximal-ideal-adic topologies, not the coefficientwise topology.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u v

namespace RingTheory

/-- A triangular coordinate change gives a distinguished polynomial, whose henselian
cylinder has the power series ring as both its principal-ideal and maximal-ideal completion.
Source: ILO, Exposé V, 1.1.1(i),(ii), 1.1.3, 1.2.3, and 2.2.3
(blueprint: lem-per-weierstrass-henselian-cylinder).

Proof:
1. Regroup coefficients as `D[[T]]`. By lem-weil-pbc-power-series-noetherian,
   lem-weil-pbc-power-series-local-ring and
   lem-weil-pbc-power-series-complete-over-complete-base these are complete Noetherian
   local rings with maximal ideals generated by the base maximal ideal and variables.
2. Reduce f modulo the base maximal ideal. Choose the lexicographically least supported
   exponent a and positive weights w_r=1, w_i=1+sum_{j>i} a_j*w_j. The exponent a has
   strictly least weight. Substitute t_i+T^(w_i); the opposite substitution is inverse.
   Lemma lem-weil-pbc-power-series-adic-evaluation gives continuous substitution maps;
   truncation and separatedness show their composites are identities. The resulting
   series has nonzero image modulo m_D. With no inner variables use the identity.
3. Apply lem-per-weierstrass-preparation-complete-local. The distinguished polynomial g
   has positive degree since f and its transform are nonunits.
4. Set A=D[T]_q. Finite-type and localization Noetherianity give A Noetherian.
   Lemma lem-per-local-pair-henselization-comparison and
   lem-weil-pbc-henselization-noetherian-completion give H Noetherian, with residue field
   D/m_D. Completeness makes R henselian by lem-weil-pbc-complete-pair-henselian.
   Polynomials outside q become units in R. The henselization universal property extends
   the inclusion uniquely to the local map φ:H→R.
5. Truncation in T and lem-weil-pbc-power-series-combined-ideal-coefficients identify
   D[T]/q^N with R/m_R^N. Elements outside q are units in these quotients. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-henselization-flat-quotients and pass to inverse limits: φ is the
   maximal-ideal completion map.
6. Apply lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-faithfully-flat to obtain faithful flatness of φ.
7. For a finite H-algebra use lem-weil-pbc-finite-over-henselian-local-product. In each
   local factor the image of g is in the maximal ideal. Idempotents in that factor and
   its quotient by g are exactly zero and one. Taking products, including the empty
   product for the zero algebra, proves that (H,gH) is henselian.
8. For N positive g^N is distinguished. Lemma lem-per-distinguished-polynomial-quotient
   identifies D[T]/(g^N) with R/(g^N), a henselian local ring by
   lem-weil-pbc-quotient-henselian-pair. Localization outside q changes nothing.
9. Lemma lem-trf-henselization-quotient-at-prime identifies H/(g^N) with the henselization
   of A/(g^N). The latter is already henselian, so its universal property makes its
   henselization map an isomorphism. These canonical quotient isomorphisms commute
   with reduction in N.
10. By lem-sbc-complete-local-subideal, R is g-adically complete. Taking inverse limits
    in step 9 gives its principal-ideal completion identification, compatibly with φ.
-/
theorem exists_weierstrass_henselian_cylinder
    (Λ : Type u) [CommRing Λ] [IsDomain Λ] [IsNoetherianRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Λ) Λ] (s : ℕ)
    (f : PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))
    (hf : f ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))
    (hred : f ∉ Ideal.map (algebraMap Λ (PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Λ)) :
    ∃ (c : PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ) ≃ₐ[PowerSeries Λ]
          PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)) (N : Fin s → ℕ)
      (g : Polynomial (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))
      (unit : (PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))ˣ),
      (∀ i : Fin s, 0 < N i) ∧
      (∀ i : Fin s, c (PowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.X i)) =
        PowerSeries.C (MvPowerSeries.X i) + PowerSeries.X ^ N i) ∧
      @Continuous _ _
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))).adicTopology
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))).adicTopology c ∧
      (s = 0 → c = AlgEquiv.refl) ∧
      c f = ↑unit * (g : PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)) ∧
      g.Monic ∧ 0 < g.natDegree ∧
      (∀ i : ℕ, i < g.natDegree → g.coeff i ∈
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)) ∧
      ∀ (H : Type v) [CommRing H]
        [Algebra (Localization.AtPrime
          (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
            (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))) H]
        [HenselianLocalRing H],
        Algebra.IsHenselizationAtPrime' (Polynomial (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))
          (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
            (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))) H →
        IsNoetherianRing H ∧
        (∃ e : (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ ⧸
            IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)) ≃+*
            IsLocalRing.ResidueField H,
          ∀ x : MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ,
            e (Ideal.Quotient.mk (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)) x) =
              IsLocalRing.residue H
                (algebraMap _ H (algebraMap _ (Localization.AtPrime
                  (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
                    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))))
                  (Polynomial.C x)))) ∧
        HenselianRing H (Ideal.span {algebraMap _ H
          (algebraMap _ (Localization.AtPrime
            (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
              (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))) g)}) ∧
        ∃ φ : H →+* PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ),
          IsLocalHom φ ∧
          (∀ p : Polynomial (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ),
            φ (algebraMap _ H (algebraMap _ (Localization.AtPrime
              (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
                (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))) p)) =
              (p : PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ))) ∧
          φ.FaithfullyFlat ∧
          (∃ e : AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal H) H ≃+*
              PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ),
            ∀ x : H, e (AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal H) H x) = φ x) ∧
          (∃ e : AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {algebraMap _ H
                (algebraMap _ (Localization.AtPrime
                  (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
                    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))) g)}) H ≃+*
              PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ),
            ∀ x : H, e (AdicCompletion.of (Ideal.span {algebraMap _ H
                (algebraMap _ (Localization.AtPrime
                  (Ideal.comap Polynomial.constantCoeff
                    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin s) Λ)))) g)}) H x) = φ x) := by
  sorry

end RingTheory
